{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_test_stress_harness", "label": "test:stress repeat-run harness", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Loops the suite N times, keeps every run's JUnit report and log, and aggregates failures by test identity. It removes ACTOR_TS_SKIP_FLAKY_MNS from the child environment by default, because a harness that inherited it would report a reliable pass rate over exactly the tests known not to be reliable."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_flaky_vs_broken", "label": "Flaky versus consistently failing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A single failure is an observation with sample size one; failing in some runs means timing, ordering or the machine decides the outcome, while failing in every run means broken and repetition adds nothing."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_hung_run_detection", "label": "Hung-run detection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A hang is data, not an abort: --run-timeout kills such a run and records it as HUNG, kept apart from a failure and from a truncated report because each points at a different cause. Without it the loop stalled on the first hang and the job died with nothing to show - the one measurement the harness exists to make."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_flake_cause_catalog", "label": "Flake cause catalog", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The families this suite has actually had, each with its signature and status: fixed sleeps, unreachable awaitCondition budgets, Bun's timer quantum, a dispatcher hop, port collisions, filesystem races, and hosted-runner worker respawn."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_fixed_sleep_before_assertion", "label": "Fixed sleep before an assertion", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The dominant family by a wide margin: N was picked from a run that passed, so it encodes one machine on one day. The conversion is unfinished - 466 sleep sites against 643 awaitCondition ones on 2026-08-16, with the sleep count rising because new tests keep being written in the old shape, plus a third helper (waitFor) re-declared locally in 32 files."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_bun_timer_quantum", "label": "Bun's timer quantum", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Windows' default timer resolution is 15.625 ms and Bun decides a timer is due on that tick boundary, so a deadline just below a multiple fires a full tick early (a 30 ms setTimeout measured at 18.67 ms idle). The clock is not the problem, the tolerance was - and there is no safe upper bound, since the same timer hit 201 ms under load."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_dispatcher_hop_between_wait_and_assert", "label": "A dispatcher hop between wait and assert", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Awaiting one actor's state and asserting on another's leaves a message send in between. The default dispatcher schedules via setImmediate, so the second actor's turn is queued ahead of the poller's next timer: a probe ran the broken condition 200 times with 0 failures at a 5 ms poll interval and still 0 at 1 ms. Real by construction, found by reading rather than by repetition."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_awaitcondition_budget_gate", "label": "AwaitCondition budget against the 5000 ms cap", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bun kills a test at 5000 ms unless it declares otherwise, so a budget at or above that is unreachable: the run reports the timeout instead of the label the helper exists to give, and the budget's own rejection lands later attributed to no test. A CI test gates largest-reachable-budget plus 1 s against the cap and re-measures bun's behaviour in a child process rather than assuming it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_skip_flaky_mns_quarantine", "label": "ACTOR_TS_SKIP_FLAKY_MNS quarantine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three suites (LeaseMajority, ParallelPubSub, ParallelMultiNodeSpec) skip themselves in test.yml, multi-runtime.yml and publish.yml. Bun on GitHub's hosted runners cannot respawn functional worker threads after the first worker test, and the same starvation delays LeaseMajority's renewal past the lease TTL into a false split-brain; neither reproduces locally or in Docker, so a green CI check says nothing about the three."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_nightly_flakes_workflow", "label": "nightly-flakes workflow", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Runs exactly the three quarantined suites at 04:00 UTC with the flag off, three repeats a night, uploading reports. It is continue-on-error on purpose: a known-red measurement must not become a red required check nobody reads, so the result arrives as a run annotation and a step summary."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_fourteen_green_nights", "label": "14 consecutive green nights", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The exit criterion - 42 consecutive green executions. A fortnight rather than a smaller number because the failure is a property of the runner pool, so it must span weekday and weekend pools and several bun-version rolls. Nothing accumulates the streak: continue-on-error rewrites the conclusion to success, and both automation routes need permissions the workflow-hygiene test forbids."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_open_flake_entries", "label": "Open flake entries", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Five intermittently failing tests listed without a verdict rather than guessed at, because ruling causes out is not establishing one. Ports, filesystem paths and short sleeps have all been eliminated, so the remaining candidates are a genuinely slow step and an ordering inversion."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_port_and_filesystem_races", "label": "Port collisions and filesystem races", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both settled and both reintroducible: bind port 0 and read the assigned port back off the listener before handing it to clients, and use mkdtemp or a randomUUID suffix per test instead of a shared fixture path."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_unquarantine_checklist", "label": "Un-quarantine checklist", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Five artifacts hang off the same cause and must move in one commit: the flag in three workflows, the three describeMns guards, bunfig's coverage ignore for the worker harness, benchmarks' --exclude=worker, and the pragmatically lowered coverage floor - keeping the nightly job as the regression guard."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_test_stress_harness", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_flaky_vs_broken", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_test_stress_harness", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_hung_run_detection", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_test_stress_harness", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_skip_flaky_mns_quarantine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_flake_cause_catalog", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_fixed_sleep_before_assertion", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_flake_cause_catalog", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_bun_timer_quantum", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_flake_cause_catalog", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_dispatcher_hop_between_wait_and_assert", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_flake_cause_catalog", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_port_and_filesystem_races", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_flake_cause_catalog", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_awaitcondition_budget_gate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_flake_cause_catalog", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_skip_flaky_mns_quarantine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_fixed_sleep_before_assertion", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_overview_awaitcondition", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_awaitcondition_budget_gate", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_overview_awaitcondition", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_bun_timer_quantum", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_manual_scheduler_manualscheduler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_skip_flaky_mns_quarantine", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_parallel_multi_node_parallelmultinodespec", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/testing/diagnosing-flakes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_nightly_flakes_workflow", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_testing_diagnosing_flakes_skip_flaky_mns_quarantine", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_scor